==> [2/3] Set up the streaming read replica (port 5433)
==> [1/8] Stop any existing replica
==> [2/8] Create replication role on the primary
DO
==> [3/8] Add a trust line for local replication at the TOP of pg_hba.conf
==> [4/8] Enable WAL level = replica and wal_log_hints on the primary
==> [5/8] Restart primary to apply settings
==> [6/8] pg_basebackup — clone the primary into the replica data dir
==> [7/8] Configure the replica's postgresql.conf (separate file, per Codespaces rule)
==> [8/8] Start the replica
